;; spec:   types §2.11, §8.3
;; expect: trap
;; trap:   array index 3 out of range 0..3
;; An array of `unit` has a length and a slot for every element, so the
;; bounds check of `array-get` holds for it as for any array (case 223
;; builds them; fibc refused them before).
(defun main () -> i64
  (do (array-get (array 3 ()) 3) 0))
